      "side": 1,
      "message": "supports_unsafe_buffers_mappings is declared inside declare_args() { ... }, which marks it as a user-configurable build argument. However, BUILD.gn overwrites it unconditionally via exec_script.\n\nWhat about moving this outside of a GN argument?  Just a regular variable.\n\n\nFor instance:\n```\ndeclare_args() {\n  enable_unsafe_buffer_warning \u003d !is_android\n}\n\n...\n\n_unsafe_buffers_mappings \u003d\n    rebase_path(\"//tools/unsafe_buffers/unsafe_buffers_mappings.txt\",\n                root_build_dir)\n\n_supports_unsafe_buffers_mappings \u003d false\nif (enable_unsafe_buffer_warning) {\n  _supports_unsafe_buffers_mappings \u003d\n      exec_script(\"//gn/check_compiler_flag.py\",\n                  [\n                    cc,\n                    \"--warning-suppression-mappings\u003d\" + _unsafe_buffers_mappings,\n                  ],\n                  \"value\")\n}\n```",
