      "writtenOn": "2026-09-11T03:19:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I thought the scope of the project was only Chrome builds, but if we want to enforce it on Android, we can do so and set enable_unsafe_buffer_warning to true; that would be very easy.\n\nIf we want to keep it as it is (enable_unsafe_buffer_warning \u003d !is_android), then the other if statements have to be modified because of the strict GN policies against unused variables.\n\nWe can do something like this:\nif (_supports_unsafe_buffers_mappings \u0026\u0026 enable_unsafe_buffer_warning) {\n       cflags +\u003d [\n        \"-Wunsafe-buffer-usage\",\n        \"--warning-suppression-mappings\u003d\" + _unsafe_buffers_mappings,\n      ]\n    } else {\n       cflags +\u003d [ \"-Wno-unsafe-buffer-usage\" ]\n       # A dummy read to satisfy GN for the string variable\n       not_needed([ \"_unsafe_buffers_mappings\" ]) \n    }",
      "parentUuid": "dcc3a9fd_9f36f886",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 23,
        "startChar": 33,
